---

<ContentLayout
  title="Save Scum Documentation — Setup, Restore & Local Storage"
  heading="Know what you’re keeping."
  description="Learn how to choose the right save folder, use checkpoints and panic shortcuts, restore safely, export archives, and run Save Scum from a source checkout."
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Documentation", href: "/docs/" }]}
  toc={toc}
  eyebrow="THE OWNER’S MANUAL"
>
  <p>
    This documentation describes version 0.1.0.{" "}
    <a href="/download/">Check release status</a> for verified platforms and
    installers. The desktop app performs real filesystem operations; the browser
    demo uses simulated saves.
  </p>
  <h2 id="folders">Choose the right save folder</h2>
  <p>
    Use <strong>Add game</strong> to detect a known location or browse to the
    existing directory that holds your progress. Steam install detection can
    fill in a game name without locating its saves. In that case, you still need
    to select the real save directory.
  </p>
  <p>
    Make an in-game save and check recent file changes. Read the path and file
    count before accepting the initial snapshot. If a restored game loads
    unchanged progress, review this path first. <strong>Fix save folder</strong>{" "}
    or <strong>Change save folder</strong> lets you detect and review a
    corrected location. Existing history remains available, and a fresh
    checkpoint is created for the corrected folder.
  </p>
  <p>
    Empty folders, symbolic links, unsafe paths, overlapping watched roots, and
    folders that overlap snapshot storage are rejected.{" "}
    <a href="/games/">Read the game location reference.</a>
  </p>
  <h2 id="restore">Restore with the game closed</h2>
  <p>
    The restore dialog previews file changes and asks you to confirm the game is
    closed. Detected running games are blocked, but process detection is only a
    hint: actually exit the game. The engine verifies the snapshot, stages its
    files, preserves a protected safety checkpoint, and swaps the directories.
  </p>
  <p>
    Afterward, review the result and load the game to verify the desired
    progress. A snapshot is a copy of files, not proof that a particular game
    version or mod combination will accept them.
  </p>
  <p>
    Original files are also retained beside the save directory in a{" "}
    <code>.save-scum-recovery-&lt;uuid&gt;</code> folder. The safety checkpoint
    records the recovery path. Remove it manually only after verifying the
    restored game. Recovery directories are outside the displayed compressed
    storage total and retention cleanup.
  </p>
  <p>
    If the process was interrupted, reopen Save Scum and review the recovery
    outcome. Monitoring may be paused for inspection. Do not repeatedly restore
    over uncertain files. Keep independent copies while diagnosing the problem.
  </p>
  <h2 id="storage">Storage, retention, and portable archives</h2>
  <p>
    Open <strong>Settings → Storage</strong> for the library location. It
    includes a SQLite metadata database, a lock file, and compressed
    content-addressed blobs. On macOS, the normal app-data directory is{" "}
    <code>~/Library/Application Support/app.savescum.desktop</code>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Use the app’s export workflow to produce a portable <code>.savescum</code>{" "}
    archive of a game’s history or a single snapshot. Imported history is
    validated before its metadata is committed and does not automatically
    replace the game’s live files.
  </p>
  <p>
    To move a whole library manually, quit the app, copy the entire library
    directory, and launch with <code>SAVE_SCUM_DATA_DIR</code> set to the new
    location. Pointing at an empty path creates a separate library; it does not
    migrate your existing one. Network filesystems have not been validated.
  </p>
  <p>
    Retention can remove eligible automatic snapshots. Manual, panic, safety,
    labeled, favorite, protected, and newest snapshots are retained. The storage
    limit is a soft compressed-blob budget, not a disk quota. Leave room for
    staging and recovery copies. Integrity verification reports damaged or
    orphaned data without silently deleting it.
  </p>
  <h2 id="shortcuts">Keep a checkpoint within reach</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Ctrl + Shift + F12:</strong> Panic Save.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Ctrl + Shift + S:</strong> create a checkpoint for the panic
      target.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Ctrl + Shift + Space:</strong> show the app.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cmd/Ctrl + K:</strong> search inside the app.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cmd/Ctrl + comma:</strong> open settings.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Global bindings are fixed in this version. Conflicts are reported in the
    interface. Tray and UI actions remain available when shortcut registration
    fails. Linux behavior, especially under Wayland, depends on the desktop
    environment.
  </p>
  <h2 id="development">Run from a source checkout</h2>
  <p>
    These commands are for people who already have the application source. They
    run from the desktop app’s root directory, not the website directory.
    Prerequisites are Node.js 20.19+ (22 recommended), Rust 1.90, npm, and the{" "}
    <a href="https://v2.tauri.app/start/prerequisites/">
      official Tauri platform prerequisites
    </a>
    .
  </p>
  <pre><code>npm ci
npm run desktop</code></pre>
  <p>For the simulated browser interface:</p>
  <pre><code>npm run dev</code></pre>
  <p>
    The browser demo runs at local port 1437. It cannot watch, restore, import,
    or export real files. A target-platform package can be built with{" "}
    <code>npm run tauri -- build</code>; signing, notarization, and public
    distribution are separate release tasks.
  </p>
  <h2 id="troubleshooting">When something does not look right</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>No new snapshot:</strong> confirm monitoring is enabled, the app
      is running, the directory is reachable, files have changed, and free space
      is available.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Capture failed:</strong> inspect the reported error. A game may
      still be writing, permissions may block access, or the storage budget may
      be reached.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Restored progress looks unchanged:</strong> verify the save path,
      selected checkpoint, game profile, and cloud synchronization behavior.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Integrity warning:</strong> keep your current files, preserve the
      library, and use an independent archive if available.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    For a save that was already lost before protection, start with the{" "}
    <a href="/guides/how-to-restore-overwritten-game-save/">
      overwritten-save recovery guide
    </a>
    . Save Scum cannot reconstruct versions it never captured.
  </p>
</ContentLayout>
